                        "entry_id": "b19c125c-1063-3639-8928-487a3def980f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The capacity of a person to worship, or to experience a religious belief"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f2b0bad4-6c06-4db9-b555-c05ff0658052",
                                "sense_id": "9027ac38-84bd-3071-9af6-34c5339bad48",
                                "text": "Here language itself reflects the feeling that the divine pathos, the passion of the \"pathetic God\" who \"yearned\" to be known, presupposes as its correlate a theopathy in the human being whose God He is."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25901a5d-1b06-43a2-95ad-4bf7b3333d9b",
                                "sense_id": "9027ac38-84bd-3071-9af6-34c5339bad48",
                                "text": "A new characteristic can be added to the description of prayer: the manifestation of self to other through speech, an agonistic speech struggling for its truth, is an ordeal, an undergoing of God, a suffering of God, a theopathy."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
